{"id":"33","title":"Hobbies","goal":"相手の興味について尋ね、自分が楽しみでしていることを説明し、趣味を始めたことや続けている期間について話せるようになります。","language":"ja","study":[{"id":"33-study-0","title":"この章のはじめに","blocks":[{"id":"ja-33-study-0-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"趣味の話は、広い質問から始められます。"},{"text":"What do you do for fun?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「楽しみで何をしていますか」という質問です。仕事の場では、"},{"text":"What do you do outside of work?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と聞くと、仕事以外のことを尋ねていると伝わります。"},{"text":"Do you have any hobbies?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「何か趣味はありますか」という別の聞き方です。答えは短い活動の紹介で十分です。自分のこれまでの生活を全部話す必要はありません。"}],"span":[6,6],"phraseIds":["ch33-p182866958124397","ch33-p270802754488685","ch33-p248124865179504"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-0-1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"活動の名前は、よく一緒に使う動詞と覚えると答えやすくなります。"}],"span":[8,8],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-33-study-0-2","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"play tennis","emphasis":true},{"text":"：テニスをします。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"play the guitar","emphasis":true},{"text":"：ギターを弾きます。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"go hiking","emphasis":true},{"text":"：ハイキングに行きます。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"do photography","emphasis":true},{"text":"：写真撮影をします。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"make pottery","emphasis":true},{"text":"：陶芸をします。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"play video games","emphasis":true},{"text":"：ビデオゲームをします。"}]}],"span":[10,15],"phraseIds":["ch33-p93078400522082","ch33-p9686439663600","ch33-p164502794525635","ch33-p253965417549990","ch33-p52295940105107","ch33-p5439663201456"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-0-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"実際に話したい活動を選びましょう。第26章には、ほかの活動の語彙もあります。ここでその全項目を使う必要はありません。"}],"span":[17,17],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch33-b2","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"What do you do for fun?"}],"id":"ch33-line10","person":"A","en":"What do you do for fun?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"},{"speaker":"B","runs":[{"text":"Mostly photography. I like taking pictures of buildings. How about you?"}],"id":"ch33-line11","person":"B","en":"Mostly photography. I like taking pictures of buildings. How about you?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034863.svg"},{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"I play guitar, but I'm still learning."}],"id":"ch33-line12","person":"A","en":"I play guitar, but I'm still learning.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"},{"speaker":"B","runs":[{"text":"Oh, nice. What kind of music do you play?"}],"id":"ch33-line13","person":"B","en":"Oh, nice. What kind of music do you play?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034863.svg"},{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"Mostly rock. A few country songs, too."}],"id":"ch33-line14","person":"A","en":"Mostly rock. A few country songs, too.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"}],"span":[10,14],"art":"ch33-scene-0.svg","theme":"hobby-chat","people":["A","B"],"caption":"この章のはじめに","phraseIds":["ch33-line10","ch33-line11","ch33-line12","ch33-line13","ch33-line14"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-0-5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Bは「主に写真です」と答え、建物の写真を撮るのが好きだという具体的な情報を添えています。"},{"text":"How about you?","emphasis":true},{"text":" で同じ質問を相手に返しています。Aはギターを弾くと答え、まだ学んでいる途中だと伝えます。Bの次の質問は、今聞いたギターの話に沿って、どんな音楽を弾くのかを尋ねています。"}],"span":[25,25],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-33-study-0-6","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Mostly","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「主に」という意味です。中心になる活動や音楽を示しますが、それ以外は全くしないという意味にはなりません。"},{"text":"I'm still learning","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「まだ学んでいるところです」です。上級者のように振る舞わずに、興味を話せます。追加の質問は相手の答えを受けて聞きます。毎回まったく新しい話題を出す必要はありません。"}],"span":[27,27],"phraseIds":["ch33-p106276438688616","ch33-p185174885875765"]}],"line":6},{"id":"33-study-1","title":"新しいことを始める","blocks":[{"id":"ja-33-study-1-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"I've started running","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、最近ランニングを始めたことに注目した言い方です。"},{"text":"I've taken up painting","emphasis":true},{"text":" も、絵を描くことを新しい活動として始めたと伝えます。"},{"text":"I'm trying out a pottery class","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、陶芸の教室を試しているところだという言い方です。今後も続けるかどうかは、まだ決めていなくても使えます。"}],"span":[31,31],"phraseIds":["ch33-p151140021316338","ch33-p251549552104240","ch33-p52688911538080"]},{"id":"ch33-b5","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"I've started taking dance classes."}],"id":"ch33-line22","person":"A","en":"I've started taking dance classes.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"},{"speaker":"B","runs":[{"text":"Really? How's it going?"}],"id":"ch33-line23","person":"B","en":"Really? How's it going?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034863.svg"},{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"It's fun, but the steps are hard to remember."}],"id":"ch33-line24","person":"A","en":"It's fun, but the steps are hard to remember.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"},{"speaker":"B","runs":[{"text":"Would you recommend the class?"}],"id":"ch33-line25","person":"B","en":"Would you recommend the class?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034863.svg"},{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"Yeah, if you don't mind being a beginner!"}],"id":"ch33-line26","person":"A","en":"Yeah, if you don't mind being a beginner!","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"}],"span":[22,26],"art":"ch33-scene-1.svg","theme":"hobby-chat","people":["A","B"],"caption":"新しいことを始める","phraseIds":["ch33-line22","ch33-line23","ch33-line24","ch33-line25","ch33-line26"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-1-2","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Aはダンス教室に通い始めたと伝えています。"},{"text":"How's it going?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、やってみてどうか、順調かを尋ねる質問です。Aの答えは、楽しいけれど動きを覚えるのは難しいという、良い点と難しい点の両方を含みます。"},{"text":"Would you recommend the class?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、その教室をほかの人にも勧めたいかという質問です。最後の答えは、初心者であることを気にしないなら勧める、という条件付きの返事です。"}],"span":[39,39],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-33-study-1-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"感想は一つの方向にそろえなくてもかまいません。"},{"text":"I like it, but it's challenging.","emphasis":true},{"text":" なら、「好きですが、難しさもあります」と伝えられます。相手の活動に興味を示すには、次の表現が使えます。"}],"span":[41,41],"phraseIds":["ch33-p234293069410178"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-1-4","type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"That sounds fun","emphasis":true},{"text":"：楽しそうですね、と反応します。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"How did you get into it?","emphasis":true},{"text":"：何がきっかけで始めたのかを尋ねます。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"What do you like about it?","emphasis":true},{"text":"：どんなところが好きなのかを尋ねます。"}]},{"number":null,"runs":[{"text":"I've never tried that. What's it like?","emphasis":true},{"text":"：自分は試したことがないと伝え、どんな感じかを尋ねます。"}]}],"span":[43,46],"phraseIds":["ch33-p34821505397999","ch33-p41276666785642","ch33-p168142667928647","ch33-p46795512455467"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-1-5","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"同じ趣味があるふりをする必要はありません。知らない活動でも、正直にそう伝えたうえで質問すれば、話を続けられます。"}],"span":[48,48],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":29},{"id":"33-study-2","title":"続けている期間を話す","blocks":[{"id":"ja-33-study-2-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"How long have you been playing?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、続けている活動について「どれくらいの間やっていますか」と尋ねます。すでに何の活動か分かっているときに使えます。答えには、"},{"text":"For about a year","emphasis":true},{"text":"（一年ほど）、"},{"text":"Since last summer","emphasis":true},{"text":"（去年の夏から）、"},{"text":"I only started last month","emphasis":true},{"text":"（先月始めたばかりです）があります。"}],"span":[52,52],"phraseIds":["ch33-p149911620160997","ch33-p155111413208582","ch33-p64636318334596","ch33-p240859525777832","ch33-p87480617071489","ch33-p248550720746406"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-2-1","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"For","emphasis":true},{"text":" の後には、どれだけ長く続けたかという期間を置きます。"},{"text":"since","emphasis":true},{"text":" の後には、いつから始まったかという出発点を置きます。質問と、自分が使いたい答えを一組で練習しましょう。"}],"span":[54,54],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch33-b8","type":"conversation","turns":[{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"How long have you been playing tennis?"}],"id":"ch33-line34","person":"A","en":"How long have you been playing tennis?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"},{"speaker":"B","runs":[{"text":"For about two years. I usually play on weekends."}],"id":"ch33-line35","person":"B","en":"For about two years. I usually play on weekends.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034863.svg"},{"speaker":"A","runs":[{"text":"Want to play sometime?"}],"id":"ch33-line36","person":"A","en":"Want to play sometime?","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034862.svg"},{"speaker":"B","runs":[{"text":"Maybe. I'm pretty rusty, though."}],"id":"ch33-line37","person":"B","en":"Maybe. I'm pretty rusty, though.","ja":"","portrait":"portrait-8034863.svg"}],"span":[34,37],"art":"ch33-scene-2.svg","theme":"hobby-chat","people":["A","B"],"caption":"続けている期間を話す","phraseIds":["ch33-line34","ch33-line35","ch33-line36","ch33-line37"]},{"id":"ja-33-study-2-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"Bは、二年ほど続けていて、普段は週末にする、と答えています。"},{"text":"Want to play sometime?","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、いつか一緒にしないかという誘いです。"},{"text":"Rusty","emphasis":true},{"text":" は、この場面では、しばらく練習しておらず勘が鈍っているという意味です。"},{"text":"Maybe","emphasis":true},{"text":" は「そうするかもしれません」という控えめな返事で、予定の確定ではありません。実際に約束を決めるには、第12章のように日時を出し、双方が合意する必要があります。"}],"span":[61,61],"phraseIds":["ch33-p227733478203936","ch33-p25167949967376"]}],"line":50},{"id":"33-words","title":"言葉と表現","blocks":[{"id":"33-glossary","type":"vocabulary","phraseIds":["ch33-v0","ch33-v1","ch33-v2","ch33-v3"]}]}],"practice":[{"id":"33-practice-0","title":"自分で試す","blocks":[{"id":"ja-33-practice-0-0","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"一人なら、質問を読んでから答えを隠し、声に出して返事をします。その後、両方の役を読みます。相手がいるなら、役を交代して練習しましょう。"}],"span":[65,65],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ch33-b11","type":"list","ordered":true,"items":[{"number":1,"runs":[{"text":"次の設定を使います："},{"text":"guitar; beginner; rock; started in January","emphasis":true},{"text":"。ギターの初心者で、主にロックを弾き、始めた時期は一月です。"},{"text":"What do you do for fun?","emphasis":true},{"text":" と "},{"text":"How long have you been playing?","emphasis":true},{"text":" に答えてください。"}],"id":"ch33-b11-0"},{"number":2,"runs":[{"text":"相手が "},{"text":"I'm trying out a cooking class.","emphasis":true},{"text":" と言います。料理教室を試しているという答えに合う追加の質問を一つしてください。相手の答えは "},{"text":"It's fun, but a little expensive.","emphasis":true},{"text":" です。楽しいけれど少し高いと聞いて反応します。自分も参加すると決めたことにはしないでください。"}],"id":"ch33-b11-1"},{"number":3,"runs":[{"text":"自分の興味、または架空の役の興味を使います。どんな活動か、感想を一つ、いつ始めたかを伝えます。その後、相手の興味について尋ねてください。"}],"id":"ch33-b11-2"}],"span":[67,69],"phraseIds":[]}],"line":65,"answers":[{"id":"ja-33-practice-0-2","type":"answer","runs":[{"text":"答えの例:","emphasis":true},{"text":" “I play guitar. I'm still learning. Mostly rock. I started in January.” / “What's the class like?” — “It's fun, but a little expensive.” — “Oh, okay. I've never tried a cooking class.”"}],"span":[71,71],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-33-practice-0-3","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"最初の例は、活動、経験の程度、音楽の種類、開始時期を短く伝えています。二つ目は、教室の様子を聞いてから、自分は試したことがないと返しています。興味を示すことと、参加を約束することを分けて考えましょう。"}],"span":[73,73],"phraseIds":[]},{"id":"ja-33-practice-0-4","type":"explanation","runs":[{"text":"後でもう一度、例を見ずに話してください。活動と期間を変えます。相手が追加の質問をできるだけの情報を渡せたかを確認しましょう。また、まだ決まっていない誘いと、確定した約束を区別できたかも確かめます。"}],"span":[75,75],"phraseIds":[]}]}],"phrases":[{"id":"ch33-p182866958124397","en":"What do you do for fun?","section":"33-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch33-p182866958124397"},{"id":"ch33-p270802754488685","en":"What do you do outside of work?","section":"33-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch33-p270802754488685"},{"id":"ch33-p248124865179504","en":"Do you have any hobbies?","section":"33-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch33-p248124865179504"},{"id":"ch33-p93078400522082","en":"play tennis","section":"33-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"word","ja":"","studyId":"ch33-p93078400522082"},{"art":"word-guitar.svg","id":"ch33-p9686439663600","en":"play the guitar","section":"33-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"phrase","ja":"","studyId":"ch33-p9686439663600"},{"id":"ch33-p164502794525635","en":"go hiking","section":"33-study-0","context":"この章のはじめに","kind":"word","ja":"","studyId":"ch33-p164502794525635"},{"art"